WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.612
Lab 2 moves to a test tenant, never
production, with fictional data.

2
00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:09.050
It uses the Conditional Access export
because it needs just one permission.

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.846
You register the app in
the tenant's own cloud,

4
00:00:11.846 --> 00:00:15.700
with a certificate, grant that
one permission, and run the task.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.819
Then you watch the token check do
its job: grant an extra permission

6
00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.938
and you get a warning, leave one out
and the run stops before any call.

7
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.013
Finally, point it at the
wrong cloud on purpose.

8
00:00:27.013 --> 00:00:29.947
Sign-in goes to the government authority,

9
00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:33.460
which doesn't hold a GCC
tenant, so it fails closed.
